position in that neighborhood and compares it to the global batch proportions using a chi-square goodness-of-fit test (degrees of freedom = n_batches - 1). Neighborhoods where the null hypothesis (neighborhood follows global batch proportions) is rejected at alpha=0.05 are counted as rejections. The function returns the kBET rejection rate: fraction of neighborhoods rejected (value in [0,1]; higher indicates stronger remaining batch effect). The implementation documents recommended k choices (e.g. between ~1% and 5% of total cells) and handles edge cases: if a neighborhood has too-small expected counts for a chi-square approximation, the neighborhood is skipped and not counted in the denominator; if all neighborhoods are skipped the function returns NaN. Input assumptions: Z is (n_cells × n_features) numpy array; batch_labels is 1D array-like with categorical labels (will be converted to integer categories). The function is pure-NumPy/Scikit-learn and returns a single float rejection rate.", "path": null, "module_id": null, "is_async": false, "calls": [], "params": [{"name": "Z", "type": "np.ndarray"}, {"name": "batch_labels", "type": "np.ndarray"}, {"name": "k", "type": "int"}], "returns": {"type": "float"}}}]\n\n请为当前计划项生成完整的 patch。\n'}], 'model': 'openai/gpt-5-mini', 'max_tokens': 4096, 'response_format': {'type': 'json_schema', 'json_schema': {'name': 'arch_augment_gen_patch', 'schema': {'type': 'object', 'required': ['op', 'target_id', 'target_file', 'depends_on', 'data'], 'additionalProperties': False, 'properties': {'op': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['add_fn', 'add_file', 'modify_fn']}, 'target_id': {'type': 'string'}, 'target_file': {'type': 'string'}, 'depends_on': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'integer'}}, 'data': {'type': 'object', 'required': ['description', 'path', 'module_id', 'is_async', 'calls', 'params', 'returns'], 'additionalProperties': False, 'properties': {'description': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'string'}, {'type': 'null'}]}, 'path': {'anyOf': [