this function treats batch_labels as cluster assignments and computes the silhouette width for each cell (using Euclidean distance) then returns the mean silhouette width across all cells. A value near +1 indicates cells are closer to cells of the same batch (poor mixing), near 0 indicates good mixing, and negative values indicate cells are closer to other batches. The implementation handles edge cases: if there is only one unique batch label, returns NaN; if any batch has a single member (which sklearn.silhouette_samples cannot handle) a safe fallback computes per-sample intra- and inter-batch mean distances using pairwise distances to produce silhouette-like scores. The function documents assumptions on input shapes and types and returns a single float (mean ASW_batch).", "path": null, "module_id": null, "is_async": false, "calls": [], "params": [{"name": "Z", "type": "np.ndarray"}, {"name": "batch_labels", "type": "np.ndarray"}], "returns": {"type": "float"}}}]

